1. What is the difference between block-level and inline elements? 
       * Block level element starts in the new line and takes the entire width
       * Inlineline element continues on the same line and does takes a specific width
2. What are void elements in HTML? Give examples. 
        * Element that contains open tag but not doesn't contains closed tags
        Example:<hr>,<img>,<br>,<input>,<meta>
3. What are semantic HTML elements?
        * Gives meaning to the tags
        Example:<strong>,<p>,<header>,<title>,<main>,<footer>,<head>
4. What is the difference between semantic and non-semantic elements?
        Semantic tags gives the meaning that can be understand by the browser 
        Example:<header>,<article>,<title>,<main>
        Non‑semantic elements are generic containers that don't describe meaning.
        Examples: <div>, <span>.
        Presentational tags like <b>, <i>, <u> affect appearance, not structure/meaning.

